evitaDB - Vendored third-party source and data in evita_engine
==============================================================

Snowball Polish stemmer
-----------------------

`io.evitadb.index.fulltext.analysis.PolishSnowballStemmer` is a modified copy of
`org.tartarus.snowball.ext.PolishStemmer` from the Apache Lucene project
(https://lucene.apache.org), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
That file is itself generated by the Snowball compiler from `polish.sbl` of the
Snowball project (https://snowballstem.org), licensed under the BSD 3-Clause
License.

Copied from the Lucene main checkout at commit b26f7672981 (2025-12-18), which
vendored the Snowball 3.0.0 output of `polish.sbl`. The Lucene release this
project pins (9.12.3) predates that commit, which is why the class is vendored
rather than depended upon.

Modifications by FG Forrest, a.s. for evitaDB:
  - Package and class renamed to io.evitadb.index.fulltext.analysis
    .PolishSnowballStemmer, so that the copy does not shadow the upstream class
    once a pinned Lucene release carries it.
  - Private go_out_grouping / go_in_grouping shims copied from Lucene main's
    org.tartarus.snowball.SnowballProgram, because the 9.12.3 runtime predates
    Snowball 3.0's generated-code contract and lacks those two methods.

No other change was made to the generated algorithm.

This NOTICE file is provided in compliance with section 4 of the Apache
License, Version 2.0, and with the attribution clause of the BSD 3-Clause
License. It states that the derived file has been changed.


Polish stop-word list
---------------------

`io/evitadb/index/fulltext/analysis/polish-stopwords.txt` is a verbatim copy of
the resource `org/apache/lucene/analysis/pl/stopwords.txt` shipped in Apache
Lucene 9.12.3's `lucene-analysis-stempel` artifact (https://lucene.apache.org).

Lucene redistributes that file from the carrot2 project
(https://project.carrot2.org/license.html) under the BSD license, which the
file's own four-line header states and which is preserved unchanged in the
copy. The list is therefore attributed to carrot2 under BSD, NOT to Lucene
under Apache-2.0.

Reason for the copy: `PolishAnalyzer.getDefaultStopSet()` reaches the same 182
words only through a static initializer that also loads Stempel's 2.2 MB
stemmer table, and evitaDB uses no Stempel stemmer - its Polish index chain
stems with the vendored Snowball stemmer above. Copying the 1.2 kB word list
removed the whole `lucene-analysis-stempel` dependency.

No modification was made to the list or to its header.
